-- Strict data: {package, target, test, owner, ledger, evidence, brief,
-- added, expires, cosign}. Dates are YYYY-MM-DD (UTC midnight).
-- Authority: maintainer decision 2026-11-22-flake-quarantine.md.
-- Only shrinks: additions are list-only PRs with ledger, failing unchanged-head
-- job, >=20 comparable rounds (<10% failures), fix brief, owner and Fable co-sign.
-- Never widen/edit an entry; remove with its fix and soak. Default 7 days,
-- maximum 14. Optional append-only renewals: [{until, by, evidence, cosign}],
-- at most two (fable then mark), each extends 1..7 days, hard cap added + 28.
-- Evidence is non-empty and distinct from entry/previous renewals.
-- Consumer contract: stdout GATE_QUARANTINE JSON is diagnostic only (children
-- can print it). Caller supplies --quarantine-out PATH, outside checkout and
-- target/. Never discover the path from stdout. Without a caller path, the
-- default is records.jsonl in a fresh 0700 directory under TMPDIR (or /tmp).
-- The pool collects in memory, then after all children, doc-tests and retries
-- creates a 0600 staging file in a private 0700 directory beside PATH and
-- atomically renames it over PATH. Parent must exist, outside the repo/build.
-- ci.mix accepts --quarantine-dir DIR and chooses mix.jsonl, workspace.jsonl,
-- portald.jsonl there (otherwise it creates a private temporary directory).
-- All echoed child lines are prefixed child: and JSON-escaped; only pool lines
-- are control output. No child receives the record path. Exactly one JSON object
-- per active entry in the selected binaries per pool run, zero for empty lists.
-- Schema: package,target,test,result,expires (effective UTC date),owner.
-- Results: pass,fail,timeout,ignored,missing. Retain all records in summaries
-- and quarantine.jsonl; append failures to the ledger. Never parse child stdout
-- as the trusted channel. An incomplete pool may leave an old file: consumers
-- must use a fresh destination per run and check the pool's completion status.
-- Same-UID isolation is out of scope: the gate executes the PR's own pool.
-- Tier 2 review defends edits to the pool/list; this channel defends against
-- test output and test-written build files, not a malicious pool edit.
entries: []
